Z||000020||artherd||11-12-2001||03:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>I find this hard to believe..my uncle larry's 3rd cousin Wilbul (who is Consequently larrys Dad)knows this guy who has a Mustang with NOS. He raced an Mclaren F1 and kicked it's ass. It will lift the tires for like 3 miles , he double clutches while drag racing , not like you granny shifitin Fiero drivers.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>McLarens don't have balls, my accord ate one the other night.  Of course, I do have 'rims' and 'an exhaust' but nothing else, except 1,000bhp window wipers. it's a real sleeper!~<P>PS: whatcha building? (electronics)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000021||Return of Fiero||11-12-2001||02:18 PM||||sorry, going to get blasted from Fiero owners and $h!t-stain owners, but im Manchester, as a kid, we would cruise the strip in Manchester. at the time, i had my first car in 94', an 88' Fiero. we would race light to light, on Elm st., just to get the short 0-40 times. EVERY 5.slow i can up against i toasted, and my 88' was a 2.5. Ballsy mo-fo for take off, never had any stang take it light to light, but on rare aoccations, we would go 2 or 3 lights, and i would lose, but not once light to light. was fun, till i raced a 95' TA with an LT1. it kind of kick the piss out of me, i was just out of the first intersection when he backed off for the next light. but hey, it want a mustang!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Myke<BR>ps<BR>no crap-stain owner ever talked to me, but everyone else did, a lot of questions about the fiero, as to speed, hp, handling, comfort. there are MANY people who say they dont like a Fiero, but want to know SO much about them. wonder why?||||reg||1
