Z||000025||2birds||11-12-2001||08:53 PM||||Make sure you have the wings for extra downforce on your wiper(s).  And get the faster yellow ones, too.<P>So if I own a Fiero GT (same one for the last 13+ years), a Mustang GT (recent addition, 94 GT, 5.slow automatic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ), and a trio of late model T-birds, does that make me bi-branded, traitorous, indecisive, or just plain confused?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Actually, I enjoy each of them for their own virtues.  The Mustang certainly isn't a rocket sled, but my stock 86 Fiero GT isn't either.  The T-birds are certainly better cars all around for long family trips (room, comfort, good handling and power), but my boys still fight the most over who gets to ride with me in the Fiero.  Go figure.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
